Error: Jet.InlineAlwaysForeign: `increment` has a foreign body, so `#Inline(Always)` cannot expand it
  --> Tests/UI/inline_always_foreign.jet:5:3
    |
  5 | #[Inline(Always), Unsafe("register-only increment"), FFI(asm)]
    |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: The body of an `#FFI(asm)` function is foreign code, not Jet: each call goes to that code, and there is no Jet body to copy into the caller. `#Inline(Always)` guarantees that every direct call is inlined on every tier, or the program is refused: sema refuses a function that calls itself or closes a cycle of marked calls (Jet.RecursiveInlineAlways), one used as a value (Jet.InlineAlwaysAddressTaken), one over the size ceiling (Jet.InlineAlwaysTooLarge), a `#Scrub` routine (Jet.InlineAlwaysScrub), one that reads `context.trace` (Jet.InlineAlwaysReadsTrace) and one with a foreign body (Jet.InlineAlwaysForeign).
 Fix: Drop `#Inline(Always)`; a function with a foreign body stays a call.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.InlineAlwaysForeign

